### User Authentication Tests
### Make sure to set your environment variables in .env file:
### JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=1h
### JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=7d
### DATABASE_URL=your-neon-database-url

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@contentType = application/json
@accessToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOjEsImVtYWlsIjoidGVzdEBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInJvbGUiOiJjdXN0b21lciIsImlhdCI6MTc2MDI3NDEyMiwiZXhwIjoxNzYwMjc3NzIyfQ.FghOy99bpMsK1BPrdNC1UcnaBuAIPNIT9N5-qvweQVU
@refreshToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOjEsImVtYWlsIjoidGVzdEBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInJvbGUiOiJjdXN0b21lciIsImlhdCI6MTc2MDI3NDEyMiwiZXhwIjoxNzYwODc4OTIyfQ.AT0UluAMmnOwQltfFmxsbbs5A3c2LsKPxz0_eKzfYDk

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. User Sign Up
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "customer",
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "phone_number": "+1234567890"
}

### 3. User Sign In
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Test Protected Route (requires access token)
### Replace {{accessToken}} with the token from signin response
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Refresh Tokens
### Replace {{refreshToken}} with the refresh token from signin response
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh/1
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshToken}}

### 6. Sign Out
### Replace {{accessToken}} with the access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signout/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. Test with Invalid Credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "wrong@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 8. Test with Invalid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### 9. Test Public Route (should work without token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 10. Create Admin User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin123",
  "role": "admin",
  "first_name": "Admin",
  "last_name": "User",
  "phone_number": "+1234567891"
}

### 10. Admin Sign In
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 11. Test Role-Based Access (if you have role-protected routes)
### Replace {{adminAccessToken}} with admin user's access token
# GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
# Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}


